# 🍱 Lunchbox Admin — Complete System Design & Limits Reference

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  ADMIN WEB DASHBOARD (Browser)                 │
│   index.html + project/js/*.js + project/css/admin.css         │
│   Hosted on: Netlify (Static)                                  │
└───────────────┬──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘
                │                      │
      Firebase SDK (client)    Netlify Serverless Functions
                │               /.netlify/functions/*
         ┌──────┴──────┐               │
   Firebase Auth   Firestore      ┌────┴──────────────┐
   (login/session)  (live data)   Supabase PostgreSQL
                                  (historical archive)
```

The system uses a **hybrid database architecture**:
- **Firebase Firestore** — real-time operational data (today's deliveries, agents, customers, live messages)
- **Supabase PostgreSQL** — cold historical archive (past days' deliveries after daily reset)
- **Netlify Functions** — serverless bridge between the admin dashboard and Supabase (auth-protected API endpoints)

