## 2. Firestore Collections & Structure

| Collection | Purpose | Document Schema |
|---|---|---|
| `users` | Delivery agent accounts | `name, email, phone, role, zone, maxDeliveries, fcmToken, totalDeliveries, completedDeliveries, onDuty, lastOnlineAt, lastOfflineAt` |
| `deliveries` | **Today's live delivery jobs** | `customerName, customerPhone, boxId, pickupLocation, deliveryAddress, assignedTo, assignedName, agentPhone, status, pickupOrder, deliveryDate, timestamp, wasDelayed, itemCount, notes, customerId` |
| `customers` | Master customer/subscription list | `name, phone, boxId, zone, pickupLocation, deliveryAddress, notes, itemCount, active, assignedAgent, routeOrder` |
| `history/{date}/deliveries` | **Legacy archive** (pre-Supabase) — Firestore sub-collections per date | Same schema as `deliveries` |
| `history/{date}/summary/stats` | Daily summary stats | `totalDeliveries, delivered, delayed, pending, completionRate, archivedAt` |
| `nobox_requests` | Customer opt-outs (no box tomorrow) | `customerId, date, reason, timestamp` |
| `inbox/{convId}/messages` | Customer→Admin chat messages | `text, from, timestamp, read` |
| `config/app` | System config (PIN, reset dates) | `customerPin, lastAutoReset, lastAutoAssign` |
| `admin_notifications` | In-app admin alerts | `message, type, timestamp, read` |

> **Daily operational data lives ONLY in `deliveries`** — filtered by `deliveryDate == today`. The real-time listener (`onSnapshot`) fires instantly on any status change by any agent.

