## 5. Supabase Limits & Usage

### Supabase Free Tier (currently used)
| Resource | Free Limit | This Project's Usage |
|---|---|---|
| **Database storage** | 500 MB | ✅ Each delivery row ≈ 1 KB. 365 days × 200 deliveries × 1 KB = ~70 MB/year |
| **Row count** | Unlimited rows | ✅ No row limit |
| **API requests** | 500,000 / month | ✅ Only admin fetches analytics (few hundred requests/month) |
| **Bandwidth** | 5 GB / month | ✅ Analytics query returns ~1–5 MB max |
| **Connection pooling** | Port 6543 (Transaction Pooler) | ✅ Used in `backfill-history.js` |
| **Project pause** | Pauses after 7 days inactivity (free) | ⚠️ Upgrade to Pro ($25/mo) to prevent this |

### Supabase Historical Storage Estimate
```
200 customers/day × 365 days = 73,000 rows/year
Each row ≈ ~1.2 KB
Total/year ≈ ~87 MB
```
→ **Free tier is good for ~5–6 years** of history at current scale.

### Netlify Functions (Serverless)
| Resource | Free Limit | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Invocations / month | 125,000 | ✅ ~1 invocation/day (reset) + occasional analytics |
| Function runtime | 10 seconds max | ✅ Sync runs under 3 seconds for 200 deliveries |
| Background functions | 15 min timeout | Not used |

