## 6. Agent Limits & Scaling

| Parameter | Current Value | Can Be Changed |
|---|---|---|
| Max agents | **No hard limit** in code | Unlimited — each is a Firestore `users` doc |
| Max deliveries per agent/day | Set per agent via `maxDeliveries` field (default 30) | Editable via Edit Agent modal |
| Auto-assign algorithm | Zone-first, then load-balanced | Scales automatically with agent count |
| Real-time status | `onSnapshot` across all agents | Firestore handles fan-out natively |

### Practical Limits
- **5–20 agents** = perfect (current scale)
- **20–100 agents** = still works; Firestore handles it, but admin UI may need pagination for agent grid
- **100+ agents** = consider paginating agents and virtualizing the delivery table

